armacraft graphics patch 0001 -- UNAPPLIED. Assign armacraft_client's custom render pipelines to Iris shaderpack programs.

Symptom (seen 2026-10-02, MC 26.3, Iris 1.11.7, Sodium 0.9.2, Complementary Unbound r5.9.3 + Euphoria Patches
1.10.5 and Alpha Piscium 1.10.0): with any shaderpack on, the ride bike, trail walls, light pool (and the arena
floor/rim/walls, same pipelines) explode into screen-filling garbage triangles. The log says, once per pipeline:
  [Iris] Missing program armacraft_client:pipeline/arma_model in override list. This is not a critical problem,
         but it could lead to weird rendering.   (also arma_wall, arma_additive; arma_solid_2s in arena mode)
Screenshots: .work/play-shaders/run-client/screenshots/bench_cu2_*.png and bench_ap1_*.png.

Cause: while a pack is active and the level is rendering, Iris swaps DefaultVertexFormat.ENTITY for its extended
IrisVertexFormats.ENTITY (mc_Entity, mc_midTexCoord, at_tangent) in RenderPipeline.getVertexFormatBinding(s) and
RenderType.format() (Iris MixinRenderPipeline, vertices/immediate/MixinRenderType), so our buffers are built with
the larger stride. Pipelines it knows are redirected to a pack program whose vertex array is created for the
extended format (MixinShaderManager_Overrides). Ours are unknown, so they keep the vanilla program and its original
ENTITY attribute bindings: wrong stride, garbage positions. They would also miss the pack's TAA jitter.

Fix: IrisApi.assignPipeline(RenderPipeline, IrisProgram) (Iris API v0.3+, present in 1.11.7) for MODEL, SOLID_2S,
WALL and ADDITIVE at client init; a pipeline something else already assigned is logged and skipped, the rest go on. Iris is a compile-only dependency (Modrinth maven, exclusiveContent so nothing else
resolves there); the Iris-typed code sits in a nested class that is only touched when Iris is loaded. OIT_WALL and
OIT_ADDITIVE need nothing: Iris forces improved transparency off while a pack is active.
render.iris_program in armacraft_client.json picks the programs (restart to change):
  emissive (default)  all four -> gbuffers_spidereyes, the program vanilla's EYES pipeline (which ours are built
                      from) goes to. Complementary/BSL-lineage packs draw it unlit and boosted, so the bike, walls and
                      light pool glow and feed the pack's bloom.
  lit                 bike, rim, walls -> gbuffers_entities (pack-lit, no glow); light pool/floor grid stay on
                      spidereyes. For packs whose spidereyes is empty: Alpha Piscium 1.10.0 draws nothing there, so
                      "emissive" would make the bike invisible. In "lit" AP draws the bike lit and the walls opaque
                      (it forces blend off for gbuffers_entities), and draws no light pool.
  off                 no assignment (the broken state; comparison only).
Known pack limit (no patch): Noble 1.9.9 forces blending off for every gbuffers program, so the additive light pool
is drawn opaque (black at its dim edge by day; reads as a glow at night). An alpha-weighted variant (SRC_ALPHA, ONE)
was tried and made it opaque lavender instead, so it was dropped. With Noble, set ride.light=false for daytime.
Not covered: the trail top edges and explosion rays use vanilla RenderTypes.linesTranslucent(), which Iris already
maps to its LINES program; they rendered correctly in both packs once the garbage geometry was gone.
Our geometry does not cast shadows under packs (it is submitted from LevelRenderEvents.COLLECT_SUBMITS, which the
Iris shadow pass does not run). IrisApi.registerShadowRenderCallback (API v0.4) could add that later.

Checked (2026-10-02):
- git apply --check against client/ as of 13:45 BST: clean.
- client jar task compiles with the patch (scratch copy, -Parmacraft.hostDir=.work/play-shaders). compileTestJava
  fails identically with and without the patch (ArmaCamSettingsTest / ArmaChaseCameraReplayTest, client/ work in
  progress at the time of the copy), so the tests were not run.
- Behaviour verified in game through the equivalent shim in .work/play-shaders/src/iriscompat (same assignments,
  done reflectively on the unmodified play jar), and once with this patch built into a jar
  (.work/play-shaders/libs/armacraft-client-0.1.2-iris.jar, bench_cu3fix_*.png): bike, walls, light pool and HUD
  render correctly under Complementary (emissive) and Alpha Piscium (lit). Arena mode (floor grid, rim walls) was
  not run under shaders. The final revision (per-pipeline "already assigned" handling) was compiled, not re-run.
Apply from the repo root:  git apply docs/graphics-patches/0001-client-iris-pipeline-programs.patch

